WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Could there be a goal that keeps us going
without becoming outdated?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
First, we have to admit something.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:34.000
There are parts of human nature
we cannot overcome by willpower alone.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Some religions teach that we can change ourselves
through self-discipline.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:55.000
It is like a world-class weightlifter
trying to lift herself off the ground.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:09.000
She can lift something heavy,
but she cannot lift herself.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:25.000
If I am stuck in the mud, someone else stuck there
may not be able to pull me out; we could sink together.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:38.000
We cannot change everything
or save ourselves by sheer effort.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:49.000
If we know a game is wasting our time,
why can it still be so hard to stop?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:02:02.000
We know some things do not satisfy us,
yet we keep going back.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Maybe it is because we have not found a better choice.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Today, I want to share another possibility.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:31.000
A God who is constant, trustworthy, and eternal.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:46.100
This is beyond human strength; this is God.
